  "bodyTypst": "#image(\"/imgs/ap-calc-bc-2011-frq-03-diagram-01.jpg\", width: 65%)\n\nLet $f(x)= e^(2 x)$. Let $R$ be the region in the first quadrant bounded by the graph of $f$, the coordinate axes, and the vertical line $x = k$, where $k > 0$. The region $R$ is shown in the figure above.\n\n(a) Write, but do not evaluate, an expression involving an integral that gives the perimeter of $R$ in terms of $k$.\n\n(b) The region $R$ is rotated about the $x$-axis to form a solid. Find the volume, $V$, of the solid in terms of $k$.\n\n(c) The volume $V$, found in part (b), changes as $k$ changes. If $frac(d k,d t)= frac(1,3)$, determine $frac(d V,d t)$ when $k = frac(1,2)$.",
